<!-- /site-examples:listen:relay -->
```

# Running one

The Deno reference relay is a single file you point at a port:

```sh
deno run --allow-net --allow-ffi --allow-env --allow-read \
    bindings/ts/relay/serve.ts 9000
# DENO-RELAY-READY 9000
```

It relays wherever a WebSocket points it, named by `?to=` or `?locator=`, and
reclaims a silent session after the idle timeout that `GLOWCAP_RELAY_IDLE_MS`
sets. Allowed targets and connection limits belong to the app that hosts the relay,
as in the Rooms
[`relay.rs`](https://github.com/jimisaacs/glowcap/blob/main/apps/rooms/rust/services/src/web/relay.rs).
The [relay README](https://github.com/jimisaacs/glowcap/blob/main/bindings/ts/relay/README.md)
covers the package. The browser peer lives in
[the TypeScript binding]($link.page('bindings/ts')).
